{"batch":1,"level":"A1","variant":"fr-FR","pedagogy":{"learner_language":"fa-IR","standard":"contemporary standard French","principles":["build directly on French Pre-A1 chunks without reteaching them","teach grammatical gender and agreement through communicative contrasts","introduce present-tense verbs through high-frequency everyday situations","keep Persian explanations concise and contrastive","use natural contemporary French while keeping beginner-safe register choices explicit"]},"units":[{"slug":"identity-and-origin","topic":"introductions","title":"Je suis français","vocab":[["francais","français","فرانسوی (مذکر)","adjective",1],["francaise","française","فرانسوی (مونث)","adjective",1],["iranien","iranien","ایرانی (مذکر)","adjective",1],["iranienne","iranienne","ایرانی (مونث)","adjective",2],["habiter","habiter","ساکن بودن / زندگی کردن","verb",2],["etre","être","بودن","verb",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Je suis français.","من فرانسوی هستم.","state_identity",["francais","etre"],1],["u2","Tu es iranien ?","تو ایرانی هستی؟","ask_identity",["iranien","etre"],1],["u3","J'habite à Paris.","من در پاریس زندگی می‌کنم.","state_residence",["habiter"],2],["u4","Elle est iranienne.","او ایرانی است.","state_identity_other",["iranienne","etre"],2]],"grammar":["Être : je suis, tu es, il/elle est","Use être to identify or describe people; adjective forms often agree with gender.","برای معرفی یا توصیف افراد از être استفاده می‌شود. صفت‌های ملیت معمولاً با جنس هماهنگ می‌شوند: français / française.",[["Je suis français.","من فرانسوی هستم."],["Elle est iranienne.","او ایرانی است."]]],"dialogues":[["À l'école","آشنایی در کلاس",[["camille","Tu es français ?","فرانسوی هستی؟"],["thomas","Oui, je suis français. Et toi ?","بله، فرانسوی هستم. تو؟"],["camille","Je suis iranienne.","من ایرانی هستم."],["thomas","Enchanté !","خوشوقتم!"]],1],["Où tu habites ?","صحبت کوتاه",[["lucas","Tu habites où ?","کجا زندگی می‌کنی؟"],["lea","J'habite à Lyon. Et toi ?","در لیون زندگی می‌کنم. تو؟"],["lucas","J'habite à Paris.","من در پاریس زندگی می‌کنم."],["lea","Ah, d'accord.","آها، باشه."]],2]]},{"slug":"articles-and-objects","topic":"objects","title":"Un livre, une clé","vocab":[["livre","livre","کتاب","noun",1],["cle","clé","کلید","noun",1],["telephone","téléphone","تلفن","noun",1],["un","un","یک / حرف تعریف نامعین مذکر","article",2],["une","une","یک / حرف تعریف نامعین مونث","article",2],["ce","ce / cette","این","demonstrative",2]],"utterances":[["u1","C'est un livre.","این یک کتاب است.","identify_object",["livre","un"],1],["u2","C'est une clé.","این یک کلید است.","identify_object",["cle","une"],1],["u3","Ce téléphone est à moi.","این تلفن مال من است.","state_possession",["telephone","ce"],2],["u4","Cette clé est à toi ?","این کلید مال توست؟","ask_possession",["cle","ce"],2]],"grammar":["Un, une et ce, cette","French nouns have grammatical gender; articles and demonstratives agree with the noun.","در فرانسوی اسم‌ها جنس دستوری دارند. un/ce معمولاً با اسم مذکر و une/cette با اسم مونث می‌آیند.",[["un livre","یک کتاب"],["une clé","یک کلید"]]],"dialogues":[["Sur la table","روی میز",[["emma","C'est quoi ?","این چیه؟"],["hugo","C'est un livre.","یک کتابه."],["emma","Et ça ?","این یکی چی؟"],["hugo","C'est une clé.","یک کلیده."]],1],["À qui ?","پیدا کردن صاحب وسیله",[["nora","Ce téléphone est à toi ?","این تلفن مال توست؟"],["julien","Non, il est à Lucas.","نه، مال لوکاسه."],["nora","Et cette clé ?","این کلید چی؟"],["julien","Elle est à moi.","مال منه."]],2]]},{"slug":"family-and-people","topic":"family","title":"Ma famille","vocab":[["mere","mère","مادر","noun",1],["pere","père","پدر","noun",1],["frere","frère","برادر","noun",1],["soeur","sœur","خواهر","noun",2],["famille","famille","خانواده","noun",2],["mon","mon / ma","مال من / ـم","possessive",2]],"utterances":[["u1","C'est ma mère.","این مادر من است.","introduce_family",["mere","mon"],1],["u2","C'est mon père.","این پدر من است.","introduce_family",["pere","mon"],1],["u3","J'ai un frère.","من یک برادر دارم.","state_family"